  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "prop:rational-certificates",
    "kind": "proposition",
    "statement": "For \\(P^\\star\\), the four SDC branch endpoint certificates are \\((x,y)=(0,29531/49500)\\), \\((0,200287/211500)\\), \\((1,54229/70500)\\), and \\((1,40731/49500)\\). Each vector has an interior coordinate, and cone multipliers \\((0,25/11)\\) certify the outer sharp endpoints; these multipliers lie outside the published normalized simplex.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "P_star",
      "r",
      "x_a",
      "lambda"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:strict-example",
      "def:branch-polytope",
      "def:interior-slack",
      "def:cone-duals",
      "thm:cone-endpoint-sharpness",
      "lem:branch-reduction"
    ],
    "justification": "Exact rational certificates prevent the strict comparison from resting on floating-point optimization.",
    "gap": "No published example isolates a legal aggregate-support SDC law at which normalization loses both sharp outer endpoints.",
    "consumer": "The certificates form a reproducible regression test for any implementation of the sharp-set algorithm.",
    "proof_tex": "Put\n\\[\n x=\\mathbb E_Q[Y_1\\mid(D,Z)=(0,0)],\\qquad\n y=\\mathbb E_Q[Y_1\\mid(D,Z)=(0,1)].\n\\]\nThe cell probabilities in \\(\\texttt{def:strict-example}\\) give \\(\\mu_D=47/100\\) and \\(\\mu_Z=14/25\\).  Direct integration of the beta densities gives factual treated means \\(79/100\\) and \\(17/20\\), whence\n\\[\n c_1=\\frac{9}{25}\\frac{79}{100}+\\frac{11}{100}\\frac{17}{20}\n =\\frac{3779}{10000},\n \\qquad\n \\theta_1=\\frac{3779}{10000}+\\frac{2}{25}x+\\frac{9}{20}y.                    \\tag{29}\n\\]\nFinite-cell covariance expansion gives\n\\[\n \\begin{aligned}\n C_D&:=\\operatorname{Cov}_Q(Y_1,D)\n =\\frac{200287}{1000000}-\\frac{47}{1250}x-\\frac{423}{2000}y,\\\\\n C_Z&:=\\operatorname{Cov}_Q(Y_1,Z)\n =-\\frac{29531}{250000}-\\frac{28}{625}x+\\frac{99}{500}y.\n \\end{aligned}                                                               \\tag{30}\n\\]\nThus the positive branch is \\(C_D,C_Z\\ge0\\), and the negative branch is \\(C_D,C_Z\\le0\\), as prescribed by \\(\\texttt{def:branch-polytope}\\).  Exact substitution in (29)--(30) gives\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|c|c|c}\n(x,y)&\\theta_1&C_D&C_Z\\\\ \\hline\n\\left(0,\\frac{29531}{49500}\\right)&\\frac{711}{1100}&\\frac{1019}{13750}&0\\\\[2pt]\n\\left(0,\\frac{200287}{211500}\\right)&\\frac{3779}{4700}&0&\\frac{2038}{29375}\\\\[2pt]\n\\left(1,\\frac{54229}{70500}\\right)&\\frac{3779}{4700}&0&-\\frac{312}{29375}\\\\[2pt]\n\\left(1,\\frac{40731}{49500}\\right)&\\frac{911}{1100}&-\\frac{78}{6875}&0\n\\end{array}.                                                                  \\tag{31}\n\\]\nThe first two vectors are positive-branch feasible and the last two are negative-branch feasible.\n\nThe two missing-cell SDC scores have common treatment coordinate \\(-47/100\\) and instrument coordinates \\(-14/25\\) and \\(11/25\\).  For\n\\[\n \\lambda_Z=\\left(0,\\frac{25}{11}\\right)',\n\\]\nthe lower-dual box coefficients on the positive branch are\n\\[\n 1-\\lambda_Z's_{(0,0)}^{\\mathrm{SDC}}=\\frac{25}{11}>0,\n \\qquad\n 1-\\lambda_Z's_{(0,1)}^{\\mathrm{SDC}}=0.                                     \\tag{32}\n\\]\nThus box minimization sets \\(x=0\\) and is indifferent to \\(y\\).  The first row of (31) has \\(C_Z=0\\), so its primal value equals the lower-dual value at \\(\\lambda_Z\\).  Weak duality, or equivalently the equality proved in \\(\\texttt{thm:cone-endpoint-sharpness}\\), certifies\n\\(L_{1,+}^{\\mathrm{SDC}}(P^\\star)=711/1100\\).  For the negative branch upper dual, the same coefficients occur; box maximization sets \\(x=1\\), and the fourth row has \\(C_Z=0\\).  Hence \\(U_{1,-}^{\\mathrm{SDC}}(P^\\star)=911/1100\\).\n\nFor the remaining endpoints take\n\\[\n \\lambda_D=\\left(\\frac{100}{47},0\\right)'.\n\\]\nBecause both missing scores have treatment coordinate \\(-47/100\\), the upper-dual coefficients for the positive branch and lower-dual coefficients for the negative branch equal zero.  The second and third rows of (31) have \\(C_D=0\\), so primal and dual values agree and certify\n\\[\n U_{1,+}^{\\mathrm{SDC}}(P^\\star)\n =L_{1,-}^{\\mathrm{SDC}}(P^\\star)\n =\\frac{3779}{4700}.                                                          \\tag{33}\n\\]\n\nEvery displayed \\(y\\)-coordinate is strictly between zero and one.  Its distance to the nearer endpoint is, row by row,\n\\[\n \\frac{19969}{49500},\\qquad\n \\frac{11213}{211500},\\qquad\n \\frac{16271}{70500},\\qquad\n \\frac{2923}{16500},                                                         \\tag{34}\n\\]\nall positive.  Taking \\(t_y\\) equal to the corresponding distance and \\(t_x=0\\) supplies a positive feasible objective in \\(\\texttt{def:interior-slack}\\).  Finally,\n\\[\n \\|\\lambda_Z\\|_1=\\frac{25}{11}>1,\n\\]\nso the unrestricted-cone certificates for the two outer sharp endpoints lie outside the normalized multiplier simplex.  This proves every stated rational certificate without numerical approximation.",
